    LLM: 'Game: Teka. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Teka is a four-player partnership trick-taking game from Afghanistan. 52 cards, 13 each. First to 104 points wins. Ace high to 2 low. Bidding: pass, ter, behi ter, or 8â€“13 tricks (or Double 13â€”win all tricks solo). Highest bidder is declarer, chooses trump, leads first trick with a trump. Follow suit; else any card. Declarer scores tricks won; Double 13 scores 26 or 52 to opponents if lost. New deal if a hand has no card above 10.',
    objective: 'Be the first partnership to reach 104 or more cumulative points. Points are scored by bidding and making tricks; failed bids score for the opponents.',
    gameplay: "1. Deal: 13 cards each, counterclockwise; dealer may cut but not shuffle after first deal. 2. Bidding: From dealer's right, each player speaks once (pass/ter/behi ter or bid 8-13 tricks or double 13). Highest bidder is declarer, chooses trump, leads first trick with a trump. 3. Play: Follow suit; winner of trick leads next. Play ends when declarer's side makes or loses the bid. 4. Scoring: Won bid scores tricks bid; lost bid scores twice that many to opponents. Double 13 scores 26 or 52. First to 104 wins.",
